    {
      "title": "Up to the Root",
      "desc": "Where the chain ends",
      "detail": "The same goes on above: .com’s keys are vouched for by a DS record in the root zone, signed by the root’s key, and that key is built into every validating resolver: the trust anchor. The resolver had those links cached, so the chain is complete: root → .com → example.com → the address.",
      "facts": [
        [
          ".com’s key",
          "Vouched for by the root"
        ],
        [
          "Root’s key",
          "Built in (trust anchor)"
        ],
        [
          "Chain",
          "Root → .com → example.com"
        ]
