    },
    {
      "title": "A Checked Answer",
      "desc": "With the AD flag",
      "detail": "The resolver answers the laptop with the address and the AD flag: authenticated data. Had any signature failed, the laptop would have got an error (SERVFAIL) instead of a forged address. DNSSEC doesn’t hide the question or the answer; for that there is DNS over HTTPS.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Answer",
          "A 203.0.113.10"
        ],
        [
          "Flag",
          "AD (authenticated data)"
        ],
        [
          "Bad signature",
          "SERVFAIL, no address"
        ]
